CORE
main.c
--bounds-check
^\[main\.array_bounds\.1\] line 8 array 'a' upper bound in a\[.*i\]: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of 2 failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^\[main\.array_bounds\.2\]
i \+ 4
^warning: ignoring
--
goto_check_c kept a constant operand of ||, && or ?: as a guard, so the
checks of `a[i]' were made again under `!(0 != 0)' and the like, and the
checks of operands that are not evaluated were made under a false guard.
